      <!-- ----- this is the interesting part of the page ----- -->
      <h3>What's new in the current version?</h3>
      <P> The current version of iRogue is: 0.40.

      <P> If you have played an earlier version of this game, you know
that there used to be two files iRogue.prc and iRogue_Library.prc.
The game is now one file (because we are at last compiling with
prc-tools 2.0 and multigen), so you can delete the old Library from
your PalmPilot as soon as you install the new iRogue.prc.

      <P> In Preferences, you can indicate that you would like the
screen to stay "centered" around your rogue.  This is off by default
(flickering is sometimes visible and may annoy) but be sure to try it
out; many people requested it.
      
      <P> You can move using the classic "hjklyubn".  This is probably
only of interest if you have a keyboard.
      
      <P> You can bind "inventory" to a hardware button.
      <P> Fixed some bugs, e.g. throwing a cursed object.

      <h4> Things that were new in the previous version</h4>
      <P> You can rebind the hardware buttons at whim.

      <h3>Bugs</h3>

      <P> iRogue seems to be reasonably stable now.  I believe it is
still possible to suffer a fatal error if you are frozen by an ice
monster under unfortunate conditions (such as being surrounded by
other monsters).  Please <a href="mailto:i0lanthe@@yahoo.com">report
any bugs you find</a> and they will be fixed as time permits.

      <P> The game may not be "well balanced" (a number of monsters,
weapons, and armors were added in a previous version).  If something
seems particularly unfair, let us know and we will continue to tweak.

      <P> iRogue comes with absolutely no warranty.  In the worst
case, a buggy application <i>could</i> force you to <b>hard</b>-reset
and lose everything since your last backup.  Caveat emptor.

      <h3>Future</h3>

      <P> Fix bugs.  Add any requested features (provided that they do
not make the game take much more memory or require a newer version of
the OS.)
      <!-- ----- end of the interesting part of the page ----- -->
